WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.100
Two days before the Obama administration

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:08.760
ended, its Department of Education

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.080
released a report showing the

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.759
administration's most expensive

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:14.130
education initiative had failed – badly.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.590
The school turnaround program was meant

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.820
to dramatically improve the nation's

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.369
lowest performing schools. The Obama team

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:22.350
sent billions of dollars to the

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.090
struggling districts running the

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.410
struggling schools.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:26.849
This is the foundation of countless

00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:28.830
previous local, state, and federal school

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.869
turnaround efforts. This final report

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:32.189
found that the schools that got the

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:34.020
money, when compared to similar schools

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.670
that didn't get the money, saw no

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.590
improvement in test scores, in high

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.210
school graduation rates, or college

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.800
attendance. None.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.600
Yes, billions of taxpayer dollars were

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.789
squandered, but more importantly, millions

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:47.160
of low-income kids are still assigned to

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.260
persistently underperforming schools. Now

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.000
the new federal education law encourages

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.590
states to use new approaches to this

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.510
problem, and the Trump administration is

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.699
pushing school choice. But whatever we do,

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:58.770
remember: The future of millions of

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.930
disadvantaged kids is at stake here.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.879
Great schools and great educators can do

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.140
so much. We just have to do something differently.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.820
To learn more about my take on

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.830
education reform, check the links in the

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.229
description below. Also, let us know what

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:15.060
other topics you'd like AEI scholars to

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.980
cover in 60 seconds.

